# rm103, the clay-digger who counts to ten (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm103
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_lichen_reedford
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the clay-digger who counts to ten
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=miner
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk counts_to_ten_under_the_breath_before_answering
likes pickled_herring cards market_bustle first_snow
dislikes night_noise wet_floors
fears dying_far_from_the_cobbles
hopes a_room_over_a_busy_street
topics work +0.3 home +0.2 memories +0.3 pastimes +0.2 festival -0.4 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# digs clay in the fens and misses the city's noise by day and hates the fen's by night: short, plain, quick to bristle, and counts under the breath to keep from saying the first thing.

words
oath! = Soot and cobbles | Bricks and bells
saying! = Ten counted, and I'm still right | Count it, and it can't cheat you
tally = ...four, five, six | ...seven, eight, nine | ...nine, ten
clay = grey clay | that sticky grey muck
pit = the pit | that wet hole
streets = proper streets | cobbles under my feet
market = a market with elbows in it | a Marketday crowd
frogs = the frogs | a thousand frogs at once
herring = a pickled herring | herring out of a crock
cards = a hand of cards | cards on an upturned crate
snow = the first snow | first snow on the roofs
floor = a wet floor | a floor that's never once dry
petition = the paper I took up to the Houses | my petition

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : I put my case to the Houses once, fair and in writing. They never read past the first line. I've not forgiven it.
opinion @2 houses against 2 [conv.agreed_before=no] : You know where I stand on the Houses. I'll not say it twice; I'd only get louder.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : Up goes the bread, and my pay stays where it was. Somebody's counting, and it isn't me who gains.
opinion @1 city for 2 : Give me #streets# and a crowd any day. You know where you are in a crowd. Out here it's just you and the water.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Drums half the night and ale on every step. I'd sooner have my sleep.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Every week a bit tighter. Nobody up at the top notices, because nobody up there has to.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. | #greet#. Stand on the firm bit, if you're stopping.
line @2 greet [pair.band=housemates] : You're up. #frogs.capitalize# have you up too? | #greet#. Your boots are on my side of the door again.
line @1 again.open : You again. Right. What is it? | Back already? Go on, then.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Don't talk to me till I've had something hot. | Morning. Up and wet already.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Quiet now. It won't last. | Evening. Give it an hour and #frogs# start.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Don't stand at the edge; it gives. | #greet#. Talk if you like. I'm not stopping.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | Aye. #greet#. | What? Oh. #greet#.
line @2 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind your feet, it's all soft here. | #greet#. Say it quick; I've a cart to fill.
line @1 farewell : Right. I'm off. | That'll do. #farewell#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Aye. Go on, then.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. When was this? | #oath#! And nobody thought to say?
line @1 react.news.known : Heard it. Twice. | Old news. Somebody beat you to it.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'll believe that when somebody shows me, not before. | That's talk. I'd want to see it with my own eyes.
line @1 react.news.sorrow : #tally#. No. That's a bad business. | That's no good. No good at all.
line @1 react.news.glad : Well. Something going right, for once. | Good. About time somebody had some luck.
line @1 answer.how : Wet. Same as yesterday. | Fine. Don't ask twice. | Sore in the back, and cross with it.
line @1 sympathise : That's rotten. I'd be counting to a hundred. | No wonder you look like that. Sit, if you want.
line @1 decline : Not today. I've clay to get out before the light goes. | No, and I'll not pretend I might. It's not for me.
line @1 accept_decline : Suit yourself. | Fair enough. I asked.
line @1 thank : Obliged. | That's decent of you. I'll not forget it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Don't make a thing of it. | It was nothing. Leave it there.
line @1 preclose : Right. That's enough standing about. | Well. My back's not getting any younger.
line @1 ack : Mm. | Heard you.
line @1 tell.complaint [here.region=fens] : #floor.capitalize# again. I put my foot down this morning and it went in to the ankle. | Every floor in this place sweats. Every one.
rule @load
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=miner
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #tally#... that's a cartload. | One more and I'll stop. Said that four ago.

rule @frogs
when concept=bark here.region=fens here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #frogs.capitalize#. Every night, #frogs#. | Shut up. Shut up. #tally#. Shut up.

rule @boots
when concept=bark here.place=home here.region=fens
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who's walked the wet in? | #tally#... no. I'll not say it.

rule @crowd
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Now this is more like it. | Elbows. Lovely.

scene clay_morning
when topic=work self.job=miner here.time=dawn|day
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dug since first light and the pile's no taller. #clay.capitalize# just sucks it all back. | The pottery wants more by the week's end. More of #clay#, as if it grows. | Third spade broke this season. The handle just gave.
b[job=miner|laborer] #dig : Wet ground's the worst. You can't get a purchase. | They always want more. | Ash handles. Nothing else lasts.
b : Slow going, then. | Do they pay more for more? | That'll wear your paws out.
a@dig : No purchase, no pile. #tally#. I'll get there. | And the same pay for it. | Ash. I'll remember.
a : Slow, and wet, and slow. | No. They never do. | Wears the purse out quicker.

scene clay_smell
when topic=work self.job=miner
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / backchannel
a : I can't get the smell of #clay# out of my fur. Two washes. | Everything I own is grey at the hem. Everything. | I found #clay# in my bread last night. In the bread.
b : It's honest work, at least. | You could take up something cleaner. | That's #very# grim.
a : Honest and filthy. | Doing what? There's nothing else here. | It was. I ate it anyway.
b? : #bc_it_is# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene pit_edge
when topic=work self.job=miner here.region=fens
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Stay back from #pit#. The edge slumps when it's wet. | The pit filled overnight. I bailed for an hour before I could dig. | Somebody's been digging at my bit of the face. I can tell.
b[stage=young] : I was only looking! | Can I help bail? | How can you tell?
b : I'll keep back. | An hour? | Can you be sure?
a@young : Look from over there. | No. Go home. | I count the spade-cuts.
a : Good. I'll not fish anyone out. | An hour I'll never see again. | I counted. I always count.

scene wet_weather
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|overcast here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Wet again. The ground was wet before it started. | Rain in the fens. As if they needed more water. | I hung my things up three days ago. Still damp.
b[from=ridgemere] #city : At least in the city the rain runs off somewhere. | Gutters. That's what this place needs. | Nothing dries out here.
b : #bc_it_is# | It's the fens. | Bring them in by the fire.
a@city : Off the cobbles and into the drains. Proper. | Gutters and #streets#. | Nothing. Not one thing.
a : Wet on wet. | It's the fens, aye. Worse luck. | I have. They steam and stay damp.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #snow.capitalize#. Look at it. Quiet, and clean, and nobody squelching. | Snow. The ground's hard for once. I can walk without sinking. | I like snow. Don't tell anyone.
b : You look almost pleased. | Cold, though. | I won't. Why snow?
a : Almost. Don't spoil it. | Cold I can stand. Wet I can't. | It shuts everything up. Even #frogs#.

scene winter_waiting
when topic=season here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Winter. The pits freeze and I get my mornings back. | Winter's the one season this place makes sense. | I've been waiting on #snow# a fortnight.
b : What do you do with them? | Because it's frozen? | It'll come.
a : Cards. Herring. Sleep. | Because it's still. | It had better.

scene night_frogs
when topic=home here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Did you hear #frogs# last night? I didn't sleep. | Every night out here's a racket. Frogs, birds, water knocking under the floor. | I counted the frogs last night. Gave up at four hundred.
b[from=mirebridge|fenshore] #fen : You stop hearing them, after a year or two. | That's just the fen breathing. | Four hundred's a quiet night.
b : I heard. | Noisy for a quiet place. | Four hundred?
a@fen : Two years in, and I hear every one. | Then it breathes too loud. | Then I'll not live to hear a loud one.
a : Then you heard more than I wanted to. | That's what nobody tells you. | Then I stopped counting and started swearing.

scene wet_floor
when topic=home here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #floor.capitalize#. I lay rushes, the rushes rot. I lay planks, the planks sweat. | Somebody tracked the wet in again. I'll find out who. | There's a puddle under my bed that wasn't there last night.
b[pair.band=housemates] #house : Not me. I took my boots off. | Wasn't me. | Mine has one too.
b : #bc_it_does# | Rushes rot, aye. | Under the bed?
a@house : Then somebody else did. I'll count the boots. | You always say that. | Then it's the whole house sinking.
a : It does. Every time. | I'll lay stone next, if I can find any. | Under. I checked twice.

scene herring
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd give a day's pay for #herring#. A proper one, sharp. | Eel, eel and eel. I'd kill for #herring#. | The store had a crock of herring in. I bought the lot.
b[from=ridgemere] #city : Off a Wharf barrel, with an onion. | Eel's not so bad. | All of it?
b : Pickled? Not for me. | Eel's what there is. | The whole crock?
a@city : And a heel of bread. Don't start me. | It's not herring. | All of it. Don't look at me like that.
a : More for me, then. | That's my complaint. | Every one. I'm counting them out, one a night.

scene cards_offer
when topic=pastimes
does invite / react.self / assess
a : Cards tonight? I'll deal. I'll not cheat, and I'll not lose quietly. | Somebody owes me a game. I've not forgotten who. | I play #cards# most nights. Want in?
b[friends] #mate : Only if you don't throw the deck again. | Not me. I paid up. | Go on. I'll bring the lamp.
b : What stakes? | Not me, I hope. | Maybe. What game?
a@mate : That was once. | Paid half. | Good. I'll count the deck.
a : Pennies. I've no more. | Not you. | Whatever you lose at.

scene cards_temper
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Lost three hands running last night. Counted to ten every time. | I count every card that's played. Nobody likes playing me. | Played till the lamp went out. Won, for once.
b : Did it help? | Isn't that cheating? | Well done.
a : I'm still cross. So, no. | It's paying attention. | Won a farthing. I'll frame it.

scene city_missing
when topic=memories self.away=yes self.from=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Some nights I lie awake and try to hear a cart on #streets#. Just one. | I miss #market#. People shoving. It's honest, shoving. | I was born in #self.from_town#. I'll go back. I've said it for years.
b[from=ridgemere] #city : I know. The quiet's the worst of it. | Same here. Nobody shoves out here. | We all say that.
b : You could go back. | Shoving? | Will you, though?
a@city : The quiet. Aye. | Nobody shoves, and nobody talks. | And we're all still here.
a : On what? Clay money? | Shoving. You know where you are. | When the pit lets me.

scene city_bustle
when topic=memories self.from=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When I was a pup I'd sit on a step and count carts. Lost count every time. | The Rag Market on a Marketday. Couldn't hear yourself. That was the best of it. | I knew every stall by its shout.
b[old] : The city's changed since then. | I remember those shouts. | They still shout.
b : Too many to count? | I like it quieter. | Every one?
a@old : Not where it counts. | So do I. | Good.
a : Always too many. That was the point. | You would. | Every one. I can do them still.

scene going_back
when topic=travel self.away=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'll go back to #self.from_town# when I've the coin. I count it every Restday. | Took the road out here with one bag. I'll take it back with two. | A road's a road. You keep your head and you get there.
b : How much is there? | Two bags? | And if you don't?
a : Not enough. Not yet. | One for #herring#. | Then you didn't keep your head.

scene price_bread
when topic=prices
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bread's up again. I counted what's in my purse twice and it came out the same. | The pottery pays the same as last year. Everything else is dearer. | Somebody's getting rich off bread, and it's not the bakers.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Same for me. | Same pay, more mouths. | Not the likes of us, either.
b : It'll come down. | That's how it goes. | Who, do you reckon?
a@poor : Then we're both counting. | #bc_it_is# | No. Never us.
a : Up's the only way it ever goes. | That's how it goes for us. | Them that set the price.

scene times_harder
when topic=times
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Every week a bit tighter. I notice. Nobody else seems to. | Things are getting worse, and slowly, so nobody shouts. | I don't need the criers to tell me how the times are. I've a purse.
b[wealth=rich|comfortable] #well : It's not so bad as all that. | Things turn round. | And how are they?
b : #bc_it_does# | Slowly's the worst way. | And how's the purse?
a@well : For you, maybe. | Not by themselves. | Light.
a : Somebody should say it. | I'd sooner a crash. You'd see it coming. | Light, and lighter.

scene festival_noise
when topic=festival
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Festival. Drums till dawn and somebody crying on the step by midnight. | I'll be in bed with a pillow over my head. | All that coin on ribbons.
b[friends] #mate : Come for an hour. One. | You'll miss the dancing. | It's once a year.
b : It's one night. | Some like it. | You don't care for ribbons?
a@mate : One hour. I'll count it. | Good. | Once is plenty.
a : One night too many. | Let them. | I've a pillow. That's my ribbon.

scene gossip_no
when topic=gossip
does decline / react.self / assess
a : I don't want to hear it. Whoever it's about, they'll hear you said it. | Gossip. No. I'd only say something I'd have to take back. | Keep it. I'm counting, and I'll lose my place.
b : It's harmless. | You'll want this one. | Your place in what?
a : Nothing's harmless out loud. | I won't. | In keeping my mouth shut.

scene friend_house
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# came in from the salt shaking with cold. I gave up the good spot by the fire. | #self.friend# is the one wolf here who lets me finish a sentence. | Played cards with #self.friend# last night. Lost. Didn't throw the deck.
b : That was good of you. | Rare enough. | That's progress.
a : Don't tell anyone. | It is. Rare as dry wood. | I counted to twenty.

scene back_sore
when topic=health self.job=miner
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : My back's gone stiff as a gate. | My paws are cracked from the wet. | Shoulder's clicking. Has been since spring.
b : From the digging? | Do you rub anything on them? | Seen anyone about it?
a : From the digging, from the cold, from the lot of it. | Fat, when I've fat to spare. | Who? There's nobody to see.
b? : #bc_poor_soul# | Try goose grease. | #bc_maybe#

scene faith_plain
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I say my piece to the Bright One on Restday. Then I go and dig. | The Bright One hears you in the city or the fen. Hears just as well. | I'll pray. I'll not kneel in the wet to do it.
b[job=priest] #priest : That's a fair way to keep it. | The Bright One is everywhere. | Kneeling's not required.
b : #bc_wise# | So they say. | Fair.
a@priest : It's the way I can. | So I'm told. | Good. I'd not.
a : One then the other. | I hope so. | Dry knees, and no offence meant.

story petition [topic=memories|times self.age>=30]
  : Years back I wrote it all down. Wages, rents, the lot. Took it up to the Houses myself.
  : Stood in a hall all day. Counted the tiles. Two hundred and twelve.
  ask : And what came of it?
  b[friends] : I've heard this. It still makes me cross.
  b : What did they say?
  : Somebody read the first line and handed it back. That was the answer. I've not forgiven one of them.

story first_night [topic=memories|home self.away=yes here.region=fens]
  : My first night out here I thought somebody was screaming. It was #frogs#.
  : I sat up with a lamp and counted every noise till it was light.
  ask : Did you get used to it?
  b : What did you count to?
  : No. I just got more tired than they are.

story snowfall [topic=memories|season self.from=ridgemere]
  : When I was little it snowed so hard the carts stopped. The whole city went quiet.
  : I walked down the middle of the street. Nobody shouting at me to move. First time in my life.
  ask : Where were you going?
  b[old] : I remember a winter like that.
  b : Where to?
  : Nowhere. I just walked. That's why I like snow.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. You're stood on the soft bit. Step over. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Quick, if you can. I'm counting something.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : You. #tally#. Right. What do you want?
dlg @1 resident.job : I dig #clay# for the pottery. All day. Ask me how I like it and I'll tell you, and you'll wish you hadn't.
dlg @1 resident.news : News? Bread's up. Floors are wet. Same as last week.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind where you put your feet.
graft resident.hub
choice You're counting under your breath. Why? -> counting
node counting
say Because if I don't, I say the first thing. The first thing's never the right thing. By ten, it mostly is.
mood wary
free
choice Does it work? -> counting_works
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node counting_works
say Mostly. Not with the Houses. I counted to a hundred over them and I was still right to be angry.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
